    <description><![CDATA[Redis is the open source, in-memory data store used by millions of developers as a database, cache, streaming engine, and message broker.

### Core capabilities

- In-memory data structures: Well-known as a "data structure server", with support for strings, hashes, lists, sets, sorted sets, streams, and more.
- Programmability: Server-side scripting with Lua and server-side stored procedures with Redis Functions.
- Extensibility: A module API for building custom extensions to Redis in C, C++, and Rust.
- Persistence: Keeps the dataset in memory for fast access, but can also persist all writes to permanent storage to survive reboots and system failures.
- Clustering: Horizontal scalability with hash-based sharding, scaling to millions of nodes with automatic re-partitioning when growing the cluster.
- High availability: Replication with automatic failover for both standalone and clustered deployments.

### Disclaimer

You should use it for local development and follow Redis official guidance to deploy it on Linux for production environment. This project doesn't bear any responsibility for any losses caused by using it and is only for learning and exchange purposes.
]]></description>
    <summary>Redis is the open source, in-memory data store used by millions of developers as a database, cache, streaming engine, and message broker.</summary>
    <releaseNotes><![CDATA[[Releases](https://github.com/redis-windows/redis-windows/releases)

This is the General Availability release of Redis 8.12 in Redis Open Source.

### Major changes compared to 8.10

- Compressed bitmaps — Integrated redis-roaring into Redis core for lower memory usage and faster bitmap operations. 
Special thanks to Antonio Viggiano, the original creator of redis-roaring, for contributing this capability!
- Substantial memory reduction for large sorted set with a new B+ tree encoding 
- New command: `BITRANGEINTARRAY` equivalent to redis-roaring’s `R.RANGEINTARRAY`, to return set bit offsets within a specified range
- Set member expiration: New commands: `SEXPIRE`,`SPEXPIRE`,`SEXPIREAT`,`SPEXPIREAT` - set expiration of a Set member; `STTL`, `SPTTL`, `SEXPIRETIME`,`SPEXPIRETIME` - retrieve remaining TTLs or expiration timestamps; `SETPERSIST` - remove the expiration of members 
- New command: `BLESS` - avoid eviction of specified keys
- New commands: `ZMOVE`, `BZMOVE` and ‘ZMOVEMEMBER‘ - atomic sorted-set moves for end-of-set batches and destination conditions 
- Count-min-sketch extensions
- Auto create JSON deep path
- Opt-in SQ8 new compression is now available for HNSW vector indexes
- `CLUSTER MIGRATION STATUS` now reports progress for both the snapshot and incremental migration phases
- Redis query engine: `FT.ALTER` avoids unnecessary document reindexing during schema additions
- Redis query engine: `EXPLAINSCORE` is now supported for `FT.HYBRID`
- Redis query engine: `RETURN_STRICT` timeout handling is now enabled for local `FT.HYBRID` execution

### Bug fixes (compared to 8.12 RC-3)

- https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/16252 HOTKEYS GET reported a wrong collection-duration-ms after 2^31 milliseconds
- https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/16219 HPERSIST ignored a replicated or AOF persist of a field the local clock had already expired
- https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/16207 Replicas misbehaved when replication compression was enabled
- https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/16267 BITCOUNT returned wrong results on AArch64 for large dense bitmaps 
- https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/16081 Addresses and names announced on the cluster bus were accepted without validation 
- RedisTimeSeries/RedisTimeSeries#2234 Fix a crash when loading persisted compaction rules with an invalid aggregation type (MOD-20881).
- RedisJSON/RedisJSONhttps://github.com/redis/redis/pull/1692 Fix JSON.ARRINSERT partially modifying arrays before returning a validation error (MOD-9116).
- RedisBloom/RedisBloomhttps://github.com/redis/redis/pull/1090 Improve TopK write performance by initializing the seed generator once, reducing per-command random-seed generation overhead.


